    "status": "present",
    "value": "Minimize total chocolate acquisition and rotation cost, allowing each type to use its cheapest price among rotations performed. The approach is: enumerate rotation counts, maintain each type minimum acquisition price across seen rotations. Its target cost is O(n^2) time/O(n) space; costs below2^53. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
